# scripts/check-legacy-naming.allowlist — exceptions for the
# 0.31.0 substrate-rename verification script.
#
# Format:
#   <path>:<line>:<token>   exact-line allowlist
#   <path>:*:<token>        whole-file allowlist (ignore every match in this file)
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are comments.
# The third field is the matched token regex as printed by the script
# (e.g. `\bcairn\b`, `/var/lib/vigo/cairn\b`).
#
# Add a line here only when the legacy term is genuinely unavoidable —
# typically: historical commit messages preserved in completed.md, the
# user's literal disk-layout path (~/cairn/...), or test fixtures that
# deliberately probe the legacy terminology.

# completed.md is the historical record — every entry there is from
# before its surrounding rename and stays as-it-was for accuracy.
.claude/projects/-home-dan-cairn-vigo/memory/completed.md:*:cairn

# Memory files live outside the repo working tree (in
# ~/.claude/projects/...) so `git ls-files` doesn't return them.
# Listed here as a safety net in case future tooling brings them in.

# Dan's literal disk layout still has historical projects under
# ~/cairn/. The substrate rename does not move his personal directories
# on disk; it only renames the code-side per-user expectation
# (~/gitmirror/<project>/) inside agent code. The license repo
# (formerly ~/cairn/vigo-lic, now ~/gitmirror/tessera) followed the
# rename — entries below that pointed at the old path are obsolete.

# The substrate-rename plan document describes the rename — every
# legacy term appears as part of the mapping description. Allowlisted
# wholesale.
internal.docs/plan-substrate-rename.md:*:cairn

# The France GTM plan lists "Cairn" as a product name in its glossary
# section; that prose was authored before the rename. Future pass.
internal.docs/plan-france-linux-migration-gtm.md:*:cairn

# multi-axis-audit.md references the memory directory absolute path
# `-home-dan-cairn-vigo` (Dan's literal workstation path).
internal.docs/multi-axis-audit.md:*:cairn

# Historical probe scripts under internal.docs/ targeting the old sigil
# subsystem. They no longer run — vigo sigil verbs were folded into
# `vigo swarm lockbox`. Kept as historical context until Dan deletes.
internal.docs/sigil-peers-probe.sh:*:sigil
internal.docs/sigil-tombstone-probe.sh:*:sigil

# Substrate audit + phase-rollout docs were authored under the legacy
# vocabulary. They describe the substrate before this rename and stay
# as-was for historical accuracy.
internal.docs/substrate-audit.md:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-livetest-all.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-livetests.md:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-perms-repair.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-deploy.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-livetest.md:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-livetest.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-b.md:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-c-livetest.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-phase-d-livetest.sh:*:cairn
internal.docs/substrate-unified-plan.md:*:cairn

# scripts/migrate-0.30.sh handles upgrades from 0.29.x to 0.30.x and
# references the older state-on-disk paths.
scripts/migrate-0.30.sh:*:cairn

# The verification script itself contains the legacy tokens as the
# patterns it greps for.
scripts/check-legacy-naming.sh:*:cairn

# CLAUDE.md previously referenced ~/cairn/vigo-lic for the license
# repo; that's now ~/gitmirror/tessera, so no `cairn` token remains
# to allowlist there.
